# KNOWN GAP (`todo/t0121`), BOTH lanes. `gg check` clean, stdout CORRECT, rc 0
# on a plain build; under `--sanitize` with `detect_leaks=1` it exits 99 with
# `LeakSanitizer: Direct leak of 6 byte(s) in 2 object(s)`.
#
# The COMPREHENSION face of the duplicate-rejection leak. `{s for i in 0..3}`
# offers the same heap key three times; the set stores one and DECLINES two,
# and the insert path drops the two it declined on the floor instead of freeing
# them. Same mechanism as `known_gaps/set_string_dup_elem_leak.gg` (the literal
# face), which is this item's original repro — this file is the second EVIDENCE
# cell, not a second filing.
#
# ⚠ IT PINS TWO THINGS AT ONCE, AND THE SECOND IS WHY IT EXISTS. The Dict-KEY
# spelling `{s: i for i in 0..3}` leaks identically (6 B / 2 objects), so the
# class is the MAP INSERT PATH and not a `Set`-only defect. The class also needs
# no comprehension at all: a plain `for i in 0..3: out.add(mk("a","b"))` leaks
# the same 6 B / 2 objects, and a `Dict[String,int]` literal with two duplicate
# heap keys leaks 3 B / 1 object.
#
# ⚠⚠ THIS SHAPE WAS ASan-CLEAN BEFORE `todo/t0841` WAS FIXED, AND THAT WAS AN
# ACCIDENT — the exact shape of a cell that is green for a reason unrelated to
# what it tests. The liveness walker used to MOVE one aliased buffer into the
# set three times, so the two keys dedup rejected were the SAME allocation as
# the one it stored: nothing was left over to leak. Now that the accumulate
# correctly CLONES a live source, the rejected clones are real allocations and
# this pre-existing defect is visible here. Nothing about `t0121`'s mechanism
# changed; the fix removed what was masking it.
#
# ⚠ HEAP-FORCED IS LOAD-BEARING: with a string LITERAL the key is a static
# `.rodata` view and there is nothing to leak, so a literal-backed probe is a
# false negative.
#
# The live SET-arm regression fixture for the `t0841` liveness fix is
# `tests/fixtures/cow_set_comprehension_invariant_in_condition.gg`, which runs
# through the CONDITION with `int` elements precisely so that it pins the
# liveness decision and not this leak.
#
# INTENDED (asserted by the wired `#[ignore]`d test): rc 0, stdout `1` / `true`,
# and LeakSanitizer-clean under `detect_leaks=1`.
# Fix at the map insert path: free the key when `gorget_map_put` reports the
# entry already existed.

from std.collections import Set

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    String s = mk("a", "b")
    Set[String] out = {s for i in 0..3}
    print(out.len())
    print(out.contains(mk("a", "b")))
